# Keep the build context to source only. `COPY . .` sends everything here to the daemon, so a stale
# build output left in the tree inflates every image build (and, before the .gitignore fix, the
# binaries were also part of the checkout at 27MB).
#
# These are the same paths .gitignore covers. They are repeated rather than shared because Docker
# does not read .gitignore, and an image that quietly embeds `./bootstrap` would ship a second
# executable nobody asked for.
/bootstrap
/seed
/e2e-all
/gitdev-ext
/sweep

.git
ui/node_modules
ui/dist
cmd/gitdev-ext/ui/dist
cmd/gitdev-ext/ui/.version

# Python bytecode a local e2e run leaves behind.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
